  "verbalization": "Myxotyroside B appears to have a shared target relationship with U251 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Myxotyroside B directly targets VMRC-LCP, which is a target of 7-Angeloylechinatine and Salsolidine. Both 7-Angeloylechinatine and Salsolidine are known to interact with U251, indicating a potential pathway where Myxotyroside B may influence U251 through these intermediaries. Additionally, Myxotyroside B is also shown to target Hepatocyte, which in turn targets Naringenin 7-O-(2'',6''-di-O-alpha-rhamnopyranosyl)-beta-glucopyranoside, which ultimately targets U251. This suggests that Myxotyroside B may exert its effects on U251 via multiple distinct pathways, possibly through different molecular mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Myxotyroside B and U251, emphasizing the importance of considering both direct and indirect interactions in understanding the drug's biological impact.",
